WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.350
Keep on holding me

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.350
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.230
I listen to your voice in your arms

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.230
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:22.040
If I reach out in the light, I can touch

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:22.040
Hikari no naka ni te wo sashinobaseba todoku

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.210
The precious arms

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.210
Anna ni motomete ita kakegae no nai ude e

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:32.220
I have been searching for so hard

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:32.220
Anna ni motomete ita kakegae no nai ude e

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:39.560
I turn around and the sky of blue

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:39.560
Furimukeba kodoku ni wa

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:49.020
Smiles down upon my solitude

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:49.020
Sora ga aoku hohoende kureru

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:56.280
In the darkness, I nearly lose sight of my dreams

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:56.280
Kurayami ni yume wo miushinai sou ni naru

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:04.210
But if you remain by my side

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:04.210
Demo anata ga itekureru no nara

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.500
Keep on holding me

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.500
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.170
I listen to your voice in your arms

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.170
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:19.350
I want to protect this love for always

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:19.350
Itsudemo kono omoi wo mamoritai no

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.680
This love...

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.680
Omoi wo

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.130
it's like they're playing house.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.960
Just what is it about them?

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.590
A Good Word

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.010
Who is it?

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.100
Oh, Minamida.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.020
What? On TV?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:06.930
Just a minute.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.980
It's amazing!

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.480
Cargo Ship Collides, 
Spins Out of Control

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:12.480
Contact has not been made with the pilot.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.980
It's a collision of cargo ships.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.200
The crew was evacuated,
but one pilot remains on board.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.780
According to the GPO Orbital Security Bureau,
steps are being taken to stop the spinning

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:28.830
but the damage to the craft is severe and
more drastic measures may endanger the pilot.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.250
Jose Rodriguez (42)

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.250
The rescue is viewed as extremely difficult.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.460
The clients are the pilot's family and colleagues.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:38.510
They were told by the GPO that
the possibility of saving him is low.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.180
The ship is on the same orbit as the Gemini Orbital Station.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:47.680
Time Remaining

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.510
Cargo Ship

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:47.680
Drifting Cargo
Ship Collision

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.720
And at this rate, they will collide in 14 hours.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.680
Gemini Orbital Station

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:47.680
Cargo Ship

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:53.610
If only he could get off the ship himself,
but communication with him has been lost.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.610
Will you go?

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.860
I already told you. I won't take on risky jobs.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.780
Not only that, I don't want to
leave the house for too long.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.200
I have to turn it down.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.620
Dr. Makurazaki is an expert in space accidents.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:15.840
Voice of: 
Dr. Junichiro Makurazaki

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.040
Well, there are a number of ways to stop it.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.710
But the critical issue in this accident is the severe damage to the ship.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.130
Which means...

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.050
What's the matter, Kurau?

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.010
If the usual methods are implemented,

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.430
there is the risk of the hull breaking apart.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.430
What's going to happen to him?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.770
This heightens our concern...

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:31.770
Jose Rodriguez (42)

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.520
...for the safety of the pilot.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.850
We'll be back after these messages.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.810
Jose Rodriguez (42)

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.810
Weather Report after these messages!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.650
TV Shopping

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.650
Hot 
Seller!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.650
<i>HOKKAIDO WATER!</i>

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.450
Kurau... don't you have to go to work?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.660
I turned it down.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.620
Why?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.630
I have to return this body to Dad.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:55.960
And...

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.630
I'll be all right.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.630
I can go shopping by myself.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.760
And I can stay at home by myself.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.180
Don't worry!

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.100
I'm so hungry!

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.680
I'll make breakfast.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.350
I found a great recipe in the cookbook.
What do you think it is?

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.810
Christmas, I'm sorry!

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.070
What?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.200
I'm... going to work.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.950
I'll be careful...

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.660
I'll be careful not to get hurt.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.660
I'm sure I can return tomorrow, so...

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.250
I'll cook something and wait for you.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.340
Good luck!

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.960
Thanks! See you later!

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:58.110
The orbital elevator, direct service to Gemini...

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.440
Ah, Minamida?

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.190
Yes, I'm about to board the plane now.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.570
Everything is on schedule.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:05.990
Yes.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.570
I'll report to you when I return.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.450
Okay, I'm cutting communications.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.000
It's me. She's about to board.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.380
The next flight? About two hours.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.420
Can you use the cancelled ticket?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.720
Yeah, if you can get on, keep after her.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.550
Yeah.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.390
Later.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.980
I'm getting hungry!

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:45.440
I'm getting hungry! So I'm going shopping!

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.800
Quite conservative.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:19.310
Hmm?

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:22.980
Well...

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.940
I-I had some business with Kurau.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.450
She's out.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.660
I see. That's strange...

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.790
Well, that's okay. I'll come again.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.340
Oh yes, my wallet!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.470
I messed up!

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.550
What the heck.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:53.970
Now then...

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.060
Teddy!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.400
Yo!

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.940
Here you are.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.530
Thank you!

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.570
Is it good, Teddy?

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:15.030
Geez, don't call me "Teddy"! it's Ted!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.910
Yeah, I know, Teddy.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.580
Ted, you're all grown up, right?

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:28.010
Geez, each time I see you, you've grown.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.090
How's school?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.590
Same as usual.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.100
How's the job you're on now?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.100
Hmm?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.390
It's going well.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.100
Taste good?

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:40.810
Yeah.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.190
Good.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.460
Say, Dad, is your new job cool?

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.670
Huh?

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.920
Mom didn't seem to like the work you did.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.710
But I liked it!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.720
I mean, it's cool to have a Dad who's with GPO!

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:14.890
Sure.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.720
It's cool... way cooler than the GPO.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.310
Here's an update on the drifting spacecraft.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:28.320
The GPO attempted to restrain the ship,
but were unable to stop its gyrating.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.780
If the craft continues to drift,

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:35.410
it will collide with Gemini Orbital Station at 20:00 hours.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:40.950
The GPO issued a statement that they will wait for the pilot to abandon ship.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:16.030
Hello. I'm an Agent from Minamida Agency.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:18.910
Are you Kurau? Thank you for coming!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.200
What? A young girl like you is an Agent?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.080
Shut up! What were we able to do?

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.710
Sorry about that. But let's go right away.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:28.380
Follow me.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.500
Excuse me...

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:35.300
Please save my husband!

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:38.840
I will.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.640
Let's hurry! Time's running out!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.390
What about permission from the GPO?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.690
We got it! We can take off immediately.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.230
I'll be at the controls. Thanks for your help.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:49.860
Sure.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.360
Ready for release.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.110
Igniting Sub 6.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.110
All systems forward.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:01.700
As soon as we're out, we'll ignite main engines.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.840
Here is an update on the drifting cargo ship.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:21.180
The ship continues to spin out of control and is
steadily approaching the Gemini Orbital Station.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.310
There still hasn't been any contact with the pilot, and concern is rising.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:29.770
We just received this news.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.940
The GPO has announced that in thirty minutes,

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:36.780
the emergency take-down of the drifting ship will 
begin despite lack of data on the pilot's condition.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:37.190
I see it!

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:37.650
I see it!
At this point, the pilot's safe return home is now...

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:39.240
At this point, the pilot's safe return home is now...

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.740
This is a warning to the approaching ship.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:45.080
Passage through this airspace
is currently forbidden.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.000
Don't mind them! Get as close as possible.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.620
We can attach a boarding bay.
At least link our orbits.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.830
What does he mean?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.920
They changed their plans.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.460
From here on out, we're breaking the law.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:56.920
So you can just stay back and sit.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.680
I can't go back empty-handed.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.510
You'll still do it?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.470
Isn't that why you called me?

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:09.310
Well? If I didn't accept,
what were you planning to do?

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.440
I was gonna...

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.900
And that's called foolhardy.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:30.000
All right, the speed is synchronized.
We're going to get closer.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.290
I can edge up real close, so just wait a bit longer.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.130
Roger that. I'm counting on you.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.630
This is a warning! Stand down immediately!

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.220
Stand down immediately!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.420
Hey, look!

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.940
These space suits are so hard to move around in.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:43.030
No good... this one's not working either.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.050
Unbelievable...

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:07.260
Are you all right, Agent?

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:10.350
I'm managing. I'm headed for the cabin now.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.440
That ship will be taken down in twenty minutes.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:15.980
Leave immediately!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.820
This one's no good either.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.230
Now then...

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.450
The ship is breaking apart!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.560
Are you all right? Can you move?

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:48.070
Am I dreaming? Have I died?

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.490
If you're dead, you can't dream.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.620
It's not spinning any more.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.370
Hey lady, how'd you do that?

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.120
I did it with your comrades.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.090
Tell me... why did you stay back?

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:19.640
Well, this is my ship... I couldn't abandon her.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:41.120
I've made everyone worry, haven't I?

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:57.260
Cargo Ship Collides, 
Spins Out of Control

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.210
Here is breaking news!

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.720
The GPO has just announced 
that the cargo ship, TSI-12,

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:54.050
which was spinning out of
 control in space, has been stabilized.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:56.720
The pilot has been rescued 
and is in good condition.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:00.560
Furthermore, although this was
not included in the GPO statement,

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:05.560
this rescue was due to the work of a sole Agent.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.560
It's Kurau!

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.020
Amazing, amazing!

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:11.280
Cargo Ship Collides, 
Spins Out of Control

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:10.740
At this time, the ship is under GPO supervision,

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.280
and an investigation is due to begin 
tomorrow to determine the cause...

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.070
What happened?

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:14.950
How did she...

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.990
Let's recap the events leading up to the rescue.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:22.710
It's me. She wasn't fleeing.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:25.710
She's quite a heroine.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:29.420
I know! I'll keep a sharp eye on her.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:32.970
Well, I just hope she goes
straight back to your side.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.550
Yeah, later.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:40.850
You're GPO?!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.860
She's unbelievable!

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.820
Trying to rescue a spinning ship is crazy enough...

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:59.370
But I understand she turned on the
thruster with all systems down!

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:00.910
It seems that way.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:04.920
I've decided to capture her as a Ryna sapien.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.830
She's not on the list.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.460
That's true.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:13.590
But she must be one, judging from the
surveillance report and what happened today.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:15.760
The higher-ups came to that conclusion, too.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.100
A Class C Unit is being assembled.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.350
I see.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.510
What is it?

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.810
Upset because I stole your glory?

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:23.640
No.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.650
Good evening, sir.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.110
And you are?

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.900
I'm Detective Ayaka Steiger.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.860
I'm the captain of the Class C Unit.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:38.410
We will be attached to your unit as of tomorrow.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.740
Steiger?

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.950
I see, so you're Steiger.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:46.580
I don't mean to be rude, but please
call me Ayaka. Everyone does.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.460
Ah, okay.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:53.670
I'm home!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.170
Welcome back!

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.600
I'm hungry.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.180
Want to eat? Or will you bathe first?

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.270
Hmm...

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.190
Bathe.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:09.520
A bath, huh?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.530
Kurau! How's your bath?

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.820
Feels great!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.740
Hey, Christmas...

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:25.370
anything out of the ordinary while I was gone?

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.330
Out of the ordinary?

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:31.080
Oh, a man was in our house.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.080
What?!

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:41.470
He didn't look like a bad man.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.100
Stay still, Christmas.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:44.560
Okay.

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:49.230
Kurau!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:58.950
Kurau?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.200
Who are you?

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:10.750
Kurau...

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.540
We can't stay here.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.420
Get ready. We're leaving.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.550
Where will we go?

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.220
It's simple...

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:26.560
to another city.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.680
Another city?

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:31.270
Dammit! I was careless!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.980
She's on to me already?!

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:33.480
Huh?

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.240
The GPO! Dammit!

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:45.700
Are you worried?

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.830
No, I'm fine.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:59.380
There's a Broker who's been 
asking me to come for some time.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:00.670
We'll go there.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:05.350
We'll be fine. We'll be together,
so there's no need to worry.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:06.890
Okay.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:13.480
We're from the GPO.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:16.440
We want to speak with you about the incident last night.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.110
Please open the door.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.990
The incident the last night?
What are you talking about?

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.110
Who is it?

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:23.740
The GPO.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:25.240
Policemen?

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.450
They don't look like patrol officers.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:32.620
What's the situation?

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.290
The terrace? Got it.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:48.890
We've spotted her!

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:49.680
Capture her!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.520
Scared?

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.530
Not a bit. I'm okay.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.610
We have them cornered on the terrace.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:03.700
We'll arrest them.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:13.710
Christmas!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:17.290
What the...

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.090
She flew!

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:25.930
So she flew...

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:46.860
From a great distance

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:46.860
Tooku haruka kanata kara

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:56.210
You smile at me

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:56.210
Kimi ga hohoemu you ni

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:05.340
The hopelessness that lingers from the past

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:05.340
Kako kara tsuzuku hakanasa

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:14.430
Is depicted in silence

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:14.430
Shizuka ni utsushi dasarete

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:23.690
Moonlight, please never change

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:23.690
Moonlight kawarazu ni ite

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:32.780
Moonlight, I'll come to see you

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:32.780
Moonlight ai ni yuku Kimi ni

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:41.920
Moonlight, I'll come running up and surely

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:41.920
Moonlight kakenobori kitto

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:51.050
Moonlight, we'll be able to meet again

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:51.050
Moonlight mou ichido aeru

00:22:53.260 --> 00:23:00.230
Moonlight

00:22:53.260 --> 00:23:00.230
Moonlight

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.910
Next Episode

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:13.620
Don't you think it would be great
to be able to fly freely through the air?

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.160
What are you talking about...

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.910
If you have nothing to talk about, I'm going back.

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.960
I heard a very strange rumor.

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:23.920
That you're after some guys
who have special powers.

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.880
Passing Through The Night
